#==============================================================================
# env.properties.aws-ol5
#
# Environment configuration for building an Oracle Linux 5 AWS AMI.
# Loaded by build-ol-aws-ami.sh via the --env option.
#
# Companion files for other Oracle Linux versions:
#   env.properties.aws-ol10  (Oracle Linux 10.x)
#   env.properties.aws-ol9   (Oracle Linux 9.x)
#   env.properties.aws-ol8   (Oracle Linux 8.x)
#   env.properties.aws-ol7   (Oracle Linux 7.x — experimental)
#   env.properties.aws-ol6   (Oracle Linux 6.x — legacy)
#
#==============================================================================
# !!! IMPORTANT DEPRECATION NOTICE !!!
#==============================================================================
# Oracle Linux 5 reached end of Premier Support in 2017 and end of Extended
# Support in 2021. It is the deepest legacy target in this directory, and the
# ONLY one whose guest cannot reach any package repository at build time:
# EL5's openssl 0.9.8e tops out at TLS 1.0, and every current repository
# endpoint requires TLS 1.2+.
#
# build-ol-aws-ami.sh works around the gaps by:
#   1. Generating distr/ol5-slim/ at runtime (env.properties, image-scripts.sh,
#      ol5-ks.cfg, provision.sh) from templates embedded in the wrapper.
#   2. HOST-staging every guest artifact into distr/ol5-slim/files/ (the
#      standard provision.d channel): the UEK R2 kernel set, the frozen ENA
#      build-toolchain closure, the EPEL5 cloud-init 0.6.3 closure, gdisk,
#      the ENA source tarball, and the AWS CLI v2 bundle zip.
#   3. Applying the same cloud/aws guard patches as OL6/OL7, plus an OL5
#      virt-install disk-bus patch (bus=virtio; the EL5 installer has no
#      virtio-scsi driver) and EL5-safe overrides of the cloud:: provisioning
#      functions (yum/dracut do not work on EL5).
#
# As a result:
#
#   * This template is intended ONLY for verification, learning, and legacy
#     migration scenarios. Do NOT use the resulting AMI for production
#     workloads. Oracle last shipped OL5 updates many years ago.
#   * The Amazon SSM Agent is a MEASURED EXCLUSION on OL5 (xz/sha256 rpmlib
#     walls + the agent's kernel-3.2 floor; SPEC B.10/D.31). It is never
#     wired, regardless of flags, and the AMI name carries no ssm marker.
#   * The ENA driver is SELF-BUILT against UEK R2 (pinned to the swept build
#     boundary; SPEC B.9/D.29). UEK R2 carries an IN-BOX nvme driver (the
#     Nitro boot precondition — measured from the kernel payload), plus the
#     xen-blkfront/xen-netfront pair as the Xen-generation fallback.
#   * Nitro boot is UNPROVEN until the real-instance E2E; Xen-generation
#     instances are the measured fallback path.
#   * Oracle Linux 5 only supports x86_64, BIOS boot, MBR partitioning, and
#     GRUB Legacy. UEK Release 2 is the only kernel line.
#
# If you need an actively supported Oracle Linux on AWS, prefer the OL8 / OL9
# / OL10 templates in this directory.
#==============================================================================

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Required] Parameters consumed by oracle-linux-image-tools
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Workspace directory for the build. Requires 20GB+ of free space.
# (Also hosts the OL5 host-supply download cache: ${WORKSPACE}/ol5-stage.)
#
# Default: /tmp/ol5-build-ws (universally accessible by the qemu user)
#
# Notes:
#   * /tmp is sometimes mounted as tmpfs (RAM-backed) on modern Linux.
#     If your host has less than ~32 GB RAM, /tmp may be too small.
#     The script will detect this and warn at runtime.
#   * /tmp is cleared on reboot. If your build may span a reboot, prefer
#     /var/tmp/ol5-build-ws or /var/lib/ol5-build-ws.
WORKSPACE="/tmp/ol5-build-ws"

# Distribution slug.
# Note: distr/ol5-slim/ does NOT exist in the upstream repo; it is created
# at runtime by build-ol-aws-ami.sh from embedded templates.
DISTR="ol5-slim"

# Target cloud
CLOUD="aws"

# Oracle Linux 5 U11 x86_64 DVD ISO.
#
# ============================ SINGLE-TOUCH MAINTENANCE POINT =================
# OL5 media predates yum.oracle.com/ISOS and the "OracleLinux-R*" naming; the
# public anonymous source is the kernel.org mirror of Oracle's original
# "Enterprise Linux" tree (5.11 is the terminal update — this URL is frozen):
ISO_URL="https://mirrors.kernel.org/oracle/EL5/U11/x86_64/Enterprise-R5-U11-Server-x86_64-dvd.iso"
# =============================================================================

# SHA256 checksum of the ISO — REQUIRED on OL5 (the build fails fast when
# empty). Oracle publishes no checksum file for this media and the mirror
# publishes MD5SUMS only, while upstream oracle-linux-image-tools accepts
# SHA1/SHA256 exclusively.
#
# RECORDED MEASUREMENT (operator, 2026-07-19): the value below was computed
# on the operator's KVM host from the downloaded ISO after the mirror-MD5
# cross-check succeeded — the full provenance chain:
#   md5sum    = 8af2121088c7e6f5ebdb6d5900403240   (matches the mirror
#               MD5SUMS at https://mirrors.kernel.org/oracle/EL5/U11/x86_64/MD5SUMS,
#               fetched and recorded 2026-07-19)
#   size      = 4222615552 bytes
#   sha256sum = b098bda92990134ea3bc8052a43b314eaffe93790a4bf872ae555b5cb467d421
# The 5.11 media is terminal/frozen, so this value is permanent. If you ever
# need to re-derive it (fresh mirror download): md5sum first (MUST match the
# recorded mirror value above), then sha256sum, then update here.
ISO_CHECKSUM="b098bda92990134ea3bc8052a43b314eaffe93790a4bf872ae555b5cb467d421"

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Optional] Image customization
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OS variant short-id used by virt-install / osinfo-query.
# The existing detect_os_variant() candidate chain tries ol5.11 ->
# oraclelinux5.11 -> rhel5.11 and settles on whatever the builder's osinfo-db
# carries (RHEL 5 and OL5 are binary-compatible).
# OS_VARIANT="rhel5.11"

# libguestfs backend
# LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND="direct"

# Build number
BUILD_NUMBER="0"

# Swap (No on cloud)
SETUP_SWAP="No"

# SELinux.
# "permissive" on OL5 by design: the EL5 targeted policy long predates the
# cloud-init/EC2 access patterns baked into this image (host-staged python26
# stack, one-shot growroot init script, IMDS fetches), and EL5 receives no
# policy updates. Enforcing on this frozen policy risks a silently broken
# first boot; permissive keeps the audit trail without the denials.
SELINUX="permissive"

# Root filesystem. On OL5 this MUST be ext3.
#   * EL5 anaconda-11.1 installs ext3 natively; ext4 is a 5.6+ tech preview
#     hidden behind a boot flag, and xfs/lvm/btrfs roots are unsupported.
#   * cloud-init 0.6.3's resizefs grows ext3 online after the one-shot
#     growroot repartition (see below), so ext3 loses nothing operationally.
# build-ol-aws-ami.sh's distr::validate() rejects any other value.
ROOT_FS="ext3"

# Root volume size of the AMI (GB).
# 10 GB on OL5 (vs 7 GB on OL6-10): the host-staged artifact set (UEK R2
# kernel + devel tree + toolchain + python26 stack) is installed into the
# image and EL5 has no cloud-utils-growpart. Growth still works: the baked
# one-shot ol-aws-growroot (fdisk MBR pattern) repartitions to the EBS volume
# end on first boot and cloud-init's resizefs grows the ext3 filesystem after
# its single reboot — this value is a floor, not a ceiling.
DISK_SIZE_GB="10"

# Amazon Time Sync Service (opt-in; default "no").
# When "yes", guest provisioning appends the link-local Amazon Time Sync
# server (169.254.169.123) as the PREFERRED source to /etc/ntp.conf (OL5 uses
# ntpd), keeping the distribution pool lines as fallback.
AMAZON_TIME_SYNC="no"

# [Optional] ENA driver user pin (emergency lever; leave unset normally).
# When set to a concrete x.y.z, it becomes the HIGHEST-priority source for
# the self-built ENA driver version: it enters the AMI name/description AND
# is passed into the guest hook. When unset (default), OL5 uses the
# installer's pin — the swept build boundary (see SPEC B.9/D.29; versions
# above it do not compile against UEK R2).
# ENA_DRIVER_VERSION="2.12.3"

# Install-time serial console. Default "no" (headless). "yes" makes upstream
# wait on `virsh console` — use only to watch the EL5 anaconda install live
# (the recommended first-contact diagnostic; see SPEC A.7).
SERIAL_CONSOLE="no"

# Enable serial console at runtime (required for the EC2 Serial Console)
SERIAL_CONSOLE_RUNTIME="Yes"

# Build-time boot mode (bios mandatory for OL5+AWS; EL5 predates UEFI
# install entirely).
BOOT_MODE_BUILD="bios"

# Kernel selection.
#
# CRITICAL for OL5+AWS:
#   * KERNEL="rhck" is NOT valid — RHCK 2.6.18 has neither nvme nor ena.
#   * KERNEL="uek" with UEK_RELEASE=2 is the ONLY combination: UEK R2
#     (2.6.39-400, a 3.0.36-base kernel) carries the in-box nvme driver
#     (class-match PCI binding — covers Amazon EBS NVMe) and builds the
#     pinned ENA driver with the el5uek shim set.
KERNEL="uek"

# UEK release for OL5 (only 2 exists).
UEK_RELEASE="2"

# Root password (debug only)
# ROOT_PASSWORD="password:ChangeMe123!"

# Root SSH public key
# ROOT_SSH_KEY="file:${HOME}/.ssh/id_rsa.pub"

# Enable cloud-init (provisions ec2-user via SSH key from EC2 metadata).
# OL5 uses EPEL5's cloud-init-0.6.3-0.12.bzr532.el5 (host-staged with its
# full python26 dependency closure; the EPEL5 archive is immutable).
# 0.6.3 defaults: user ec2-user / disable_root 1 / plain IMDSv1 DataSourceEc2.
#
# CLOUD_USER is PINNED to ec2-user on OL5: cloud-init 0.6.3 has no
# users-groups module (it cannot create accounts), so the synthesized
# kickstart pre-creates exactly ec2-user; the wrapper overrides any other
# value with a warning.
CLOUD_INIT="Yes"
CLOUD_USER="ec2-user"

# RPM update policy applied during provisioning.
# "no" is MANDATORY on OL5 (distr::validate rejects anything else): the guest
# has no reachable repository (EL5 = TLS 1.0 max), so there is nothing to
# update from. The image ships the ISO package set plus the host-staged
# artifacts, exactly as pinned.
UPDATE_TO_LATEST="no"

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [Required] AWS import parameters
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Region in which the AMI will be created.
# Empty = auto-resolve (IMDSv2 -> IMDSv1 -> "ap-northeast-1" fallback).
AWS_REGION=""

# S3 bucket used as the staging area for the VMDK upload.
# Shared across all OL versions in this directory; S3_KEY_PREFIX isolates
# this version.
S3_BUCKET="my-oracle-linux-ami-import-bucket"
S3_KEY_PREFIX="ol5-ami-import"

# AMI_NAME="OracleLinux-5-U11-x86_64-$(date +%Y%m%d)"
# AMI_DESCRIPTION="Oracle Linux 5 Update 11 (x86_64) custom AMI"

# AMI boot mode.
# OL5 produces legacy-bios only (no UEFI / NitroTPM / Secure Boot).
BOOT_MODE="legacy-bios"

VMIMPORT_ROLE_NAME="vmimport"
